Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 02:53:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sources: record lane-158 PrismML K-cache disposition

Origin: PrismML v6 dea384100..b075a360c plus 4dd165625
Measured-effect: source census corrected; native model effect UNMEASURED (HQ-OWED)
---
 tools/arifi-sync/sources.json | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/tools/arifi-sync/sources.json b/tools/arifi-sync/sources.json
index cf6effa13..dd8135cfd 100644
--- a/tools/arifi-sync/sources.json
+++ b/tools/arifi-sync/sources.json
@@ -119,6 +119,7 @@
       "url": "https://github.com/PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp",
       "ref": "prisml/prism",
       "pin": "7529fdaaf",
+      "pin_review_2026_08_19_lane158": "PIN DELIBERATELY HELD at 7529fdaaf while lane-158 TAKES the K-cache mean-centering capability from PrismML's separate v6 lineage and the default-branch follow-up 4dd165625. SOURCE-CENSUS CORRECTION: the lane brief's `1076 new lines in 8 files` is exact only for the EIGHT wholly new files; the full feature range dea384100^..b075a360c is 1377 insertions / 2 deletions across 19 files, with ELEVEN existing touchpoints (the brief and lane-156 review said eight). Every one of the eight new files was read in full and the complete feature-range diff over the eleven existing files was reviewed before porting. TAKEN onto kcache158/2026-08-19 in four source commits: 6b9a2e121 (compile flag GGML_ARIFI_KV_MEANCENTER, default OFF, port), 932d33fe1 (ArifiLabs hardening: domain-separated SHA-256 over every byte of every ordered GGUF split; calibration schema/model/k_rot/geometry checks; missing, partial, extra, wrong-model and wrong-basis artifacts refuse load), 8a05ba3c8 (4dd165625 re-derived at this fork's centralized speculative-params seam so an external draft context never inherits the target calibration), and f56cf26f1 (Vulkan pre/post tensor probe plus bench-pure, three-replication A/B runner/verifier). The upstream 4dd fix was NOT silently treated as part of v6: it is not an ancestor of b075a360c and was audited/applied separately. PIN WHY HELD: tools/arifi-sync tracks the real default ref prisml/prism, whose tip also contains 9ca265a57; that CUDA __byte_perm candidate remains the structural, post-refactor mmq-load-tiles.cuh manual-port blocker documented by lane-156. Advancing to the ref tip would falsely close that blocked TAKE, while changing the ref would violate the registered-default-branch contract and hide default-branch drift. SOURCE/HARNESS EFFECT CHECKED: patch-series generation/check/replay and arifi_sync_check are GREEN; Python A/B verifier selftest accepts a good fixture and returns RED on a planted overlap. NATIVE BUILD, OFF byte identity, exact-model calibration, Vulkan tensor execution, PPL, decode speed, full backend sweep, and independent checker remain UNMEASURED in this managed seat and are explicitly HQ-OWNED; no accuracy, speed, or context-raise claim is made here.",
       "pin_review_2026_08_18_lane156": "PIN DELIBERATELY HELD at 7529fdaaf for the SECOND wave, and the reason is now SHARPER than lane-152's, not merely repeated. Both commits in 7529fdaaf..9ca265a57 were re-reviewed against arifi/main at b10488. (1) 4dd165625 'server: do not propagate kv-mean-center bias to draft model contexts' - SKIP-UNTIL-FEATURE, re-CHECKED at this tip: `kv_mean_center` appears in our tree in exactly THREE places and every one of them is pin-review prose (tools/arifi-sync/sources.json and two banked patch files). Zero code. The fix patches a prisml capability we have never ingested; it rides in with the feature and never before it. (2) 9ca265a57 'cuda: extract Q2_0 elements via __byte_perm' - A REAL TAKE CANDIDATE ON OUR OWN TYPE, BLOCKED, and the blocker is now NAMED with the file: `git apply --3way` reaches 'Applied with conflicts' on BOTH files. vecdotq.cuh conflicts are COMMENT-ONLY (3 hunks, all comment text) - that half is portable. mmq.cuh is the blocker and it is STRUCTURAL, not textual: prisml's own commit message says 'Upstream's tile-load lives in mmq-load-tiles.cuh after their MMQ refactor; ours is still in mmq.cuh, so this is a manual port'. WE ARE ON THE POST-REFACTOR SIDE - our load_tiles_q2_0 is in ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq-load-tiles.cuh (which prisml does not have as a file at all) and our mmq-load-tiles.cuh:114-117 carries the QK2_0 blocks_per_iter/scale_entries arithmetic. So their manual port must be RE-DERIVED against mmq-load-tiles.cuh; it cannot be applied. THE PIN IS HELD RATHER THAN ADVANCED because the runbook only allows a re-pin for SKIP, and this is a blocked TAKE, not a SKIP. The unblocking work is bounded: re-derive the __byte_perm decode against our mmq-load-tiles.cuh load_tiles_q2_0 plus the (already-clean) vecdotq.cuh half. It is CUDA, so it lands unbuilt under the standing 2026-08-18 HQ off-rig ruling and carries NO measurement on this Vulkan-only rig. THE v6 / K-CACHE-MEAN-CENTER VERDICT ORDERED BY LANE-156: **DEFERRED, WITH THE COST NAMED - explicitly NOT declined.** It is backend-agnostic and would therefore work on our Vulkan path (their src/llama-kv-cache.cpp:1304 states the mean is subtracted before K is written and 'nothing else in attention needs to change'), so it is a genuine accuracy lever for quantized KV here. THE COST, MEASURED at prisml/prism against merge-base 8a963fc10: 1076 NEW lines in files we do not have (common/kv-mean-center.cpp 76, common/kv-mean-center.h 30, tools/kv-mean-center/kv-mean-center.cpp 305, tools/kv-mean-center/make-calib-corpus.sh 126, tools/kv-mean-center/README.md 91, tools/kv-mean-center/CMakeLists.txt 8, tests/test-kv-mean-center.cpp 338, docs/kv-mean-center.md 102) PLUS touchpoints in EIGHT shared files (common/arg.cpp, common/common.cpp, common/common.h, include/llama.h, src/llama-context.cpp x6, src/llama-kv-cache.cpp x5, src/llama-kv-cache.h x2, tools/server/server-context.cpp x2) PLUS a PER-MODEL operational cost that no other ingest in this fork has: the feature is inert without a calibration bias GGUF, so every model we want it on needs a calib corpus built and the tool run, and its accuracy claim is unmeasured here until that exists. ORDER OF WORK when it is taken: common/kv-mean-center.{h,cpp} -> the llama-kv-cache load/apply legs -> arg/common wiring -> the tool -> tests -> THEN 4dd165625 -> then one measured q4_0-KV accuracy run on this rig, which is the only number that can justify it. This is a lane, not a rung.",
       "pin_review_2026_08_18_lane152": "PIN DELIBERATELY STILL NOT ADVANCED, consistent with the lane-143 key below and with ciru in this same file. Both commits in 7529fdaaf..9ca265a57 were re-reviewed against our tree at b10481 and NEITHER is closed. 4dd165625 'server: do not propagate kv-mean-center bias to draft model contexts' is DEFERRED, NOT DECLINED, and the distinction is the point: `kv_mean_center_path` does not exist anywhere in our tools/server/server-context.cpp - CHECKED - so the fix patches a prisml capability we have never ingested and there is nothing here for it to fix. The K-cache mean-center bias FEATURE is the real item; this fix rides in with it, never before it. 9ca265a57 'cuda: extract Q2_0 elements via __byte_perm' is a live candidate on OUR type (Q2_0 is ours) and is NOT declined for being CUDA - the union law forbids that reason class and this fork ships CUDA source - it is simply not ported yet. And the lane-143 warning stands unchanged and is the bigger number: the ENTIRE v6 line (prism-v6, prism-v6-g128-arm-metal-fixes, prism-v6-dspark-dflash, feat/tq1_0-cuda, fix/metal-im2col-dispatch-wide-set-rows) is invisible to this ref, so the BEHIND-by-2 this row produces UNDERSTATES the backlog. A BEHIND row is a live signal; `current` here would be a false one.",
       "pin_review_2026_08_17_lane143": "PIN DELIBERATELY NOT ADVANCED, and this entry is the reason. I DID review 7529fdaaf..9ca265a57 (below) and briefly advanced the pin to 9ca265a57 - then reverted it, because advancing made `currency` print 'prisml ... current' while the fork's actual unreviewed work sits on branches this ref never sees. currency's table is what a reader acts on; a pin_review body is not. A green row that has to be corrected by prose is worse than a BEHIND row, and it would contradict the reasoning that keeps ciru pinned back in this same file. The BEHIND-by-2 this produces UNDERSTATES the real backlog, which is the v6 line - but BEHIND is a live signal and current is a false one. Reviewed 7529fdaaf..9ca265a57, 2 commits, both fork-authored: 4dd165625 'server: do not propagate kv-mean-center bias to draft model contexts (#81)' (a real correctness fix on a path we run - worth reading) and 9ca265a57 'cuda: extract Q2_0 elements via __byte_perm (#104)' (CUDA, skip, this box is Vulkan). WARNING - THE SMALL NUMBER IS MISLEADING, and this is the one fork where the 'default branch understates' defect is REAL (it is not real for tq3, which is where the register previously claimed it): prisml/prism last moved 2026-07-31, while the fork has fix/metal-im2col-dispatch-wide-set-rows at 2026-08-16, feat/tq1_0-cuda at 2026-08-13, prism-v6-g128-arm-metal-fixes at 2026-08-11, and prism-v6 + prism-v6-dspark-dflash at 2026-08-10. The ENTIRE v6 line is invisible to this pin. CONTRACT FLAG D: prisml/prism-v6 moved Q2_0_G128 to type id 142 with geometry (128, 2+32) - byte-for-byte our g128 - and it IS in their gguf-py. 142 is free for us so there is no collision, but TYPE-ID-ALLOCATION.md section 5's premise 'PrismML shipped 128-value-per-block data under type-id 42' no longer describes their current line, and the g128 gate's whole rationale rests on that premise. Note prisml/prism itself has NO g128 in its enum at all (COUNT=43). The `ref` was NOT changed: prism is the true default branch and this file's _comment is emphatic about not guessing a branch, but the work is elsewhere - that is a register-semantics call for HQ, above a review lane.",
